is Aquinas chapter in Anscombe and Geach, Three Philosophers; Geach is","transcription_status":"human_verified","typography_status":"human_verified"},{"bbox":[300,1240,2187,1286],"canonical_reference":null,"column_id":"notes","content_class":"footnote","geometry_status":"human_verified","hierarchy_level":null,"inline_spans":[],"language":"eng","leaf_id":"single","line_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-native-0015","note_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-note-43","paragraph_role":"continuation","reading_order":15,"source":"human","structure_status":"human_verified","text":"mostly trying to save and interpret Thomas Aquinas on the act of being and on God as his own esse, and to show","transcription_status":"human_verified","typography_status":"human_verified"},{"bbox":[300,1288,2181,1334],"canonical_reference":null,"column_id":"notes","content_class":"footnote","geometry_status":"human_verified","hierarchy_level":null,"inline_spans":[],"language":"eng","leaf_id":"single","line_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-native-0016","note_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-note-43","paragraph_role":"continuation","reading_order":16,"source":"human","structure_status":"human_verified","text":"that Thomism is not refuted by Frege's analysis of existence. Geach's distinction between two kinds of being is a","transcription_status":"human_verified","typography_status":"human_verified"},{"bbox":[300,1336,2117,1382],"canonical_reference":null,"column_id":"notes","content_class":"footnote","geometry_status":"human_verified","hierarchy_level":null,"inline_spans":[],"language":"eng","leaf_id":"single","line_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-native-0017","note_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-note-43","paragraph_role":"continuation","reading_order":17,"source":"human","structure_status":"human_verified","text":"version of Thomas' distinction between two senses of being as existence, one which is the being-as-actuality","transcription_status":"human_verified","typography_status":"human_verified"},{"bbox":[300,1384,2217,1430],"canonical_reference":null,"column_id":"notes","content_class":"footnote","geometry_status":"human_verified","hierarchy_level":null,"inline_spans":[],"language":"eng","leaf_id":"single","line_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-native-0018","note_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-note-43","paragraph_role":"continuation","reading_order":18,"source":"human","structure_status":"human_verified","text":"completing the being-as-potentiality which is categorial being, and the other which is being-as-truth. this in turn is","transcription_status":"human_verified","typography_status":"human_verified"},{"bbox":[300,1431,2082,1477],"canonical_reference":null,"column_id":"notes","content_class":"footnote","geometry_status":"human_verified","hierarchy_level":null,"inline_spans":[],"language":"eng","leaf_id":"single","line_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-native-0019","note_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-note-43","paragraph_role":"continuation","reading_order":19,"source":"human","structure_status":"human_verified","text":"part of Thomas' response to Fârâbî's and Averroes' criticisms of theories (Kindi's [following Proclus]--and","transcription_status":"human_verified","typography_status":"human_verified"},{"bbox":[300,1479,2246,1525],"canonical_reference":null,"column_id":"notes","content_class":"footnote","geometry_status":"human_verified","hierarchy_level":null,"inline_spans":[],"language":"eng","leaf_id":"single","line_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-native-0020","note_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-note-43","paragraph_role":"continuation","reading_order":20,"source":"human","structure_status":"human_verified","text":"Avicenna's respectively) on which things other than God exist, not through themselves, but by participating in being","transcription_status":"human_verified","typography_status":"human_verified"},{"bbox":[300,1527,2165,1573],"canonical_reference":null,"column_id":"notes","content_class":"footnote","geometry_status":"human_verified","hierarchy_level":null,"inline_spans":[],"language":"eng","leaf_id":"single","line_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-native-0021","note_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-note-43","paragraph_role":"continuation","reading_order":21,"source":"human","structure_status":"human_verified","text":"(identified with God by Kindi but not by Avicenna). Fârâbî and Averroes distinguish between two senses of (1-","transcription_status":"human_verified","typography_status":"human_verified"},{"bbox":[300,1575,2235,1621],"canonical_reference":null,"column_id":"notes","content_class":"footnote","geometry_status":"human_verified","hierarchy_level":null,"inline_spans":[],"language":"eng","leaf_id":"single","line_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-native-0022","note_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-note-43","paragraph_role":"continuation","reading_order":22,"source":"human","structure_status":"human_verified","text":"place) being, categorial being, which is real but equivocal across the categories and predicates of each thing its own","transcription_status":"human_verified","typography_status":"human_verified"},{"bbox":[300,1623,2221,1669],"canonical_reference":null,"column_id":"notes","content_class":"footnote","geometry_status":"human_verified","hierarchy_level":null,"inline_spans":[],"language":"eng","leaf_id":"single","line_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-native-0023","note_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-note-43","paragraph_role":"continuation","reading_order":23,"source":"human","structure_status":"human_verified","text":"essence (so not a separate being for things in the different categories to participate in), and being-as-truth, which is","transcription_status":"human_verified","typography_status":"human_verified"},{"bbox":[300,1671,2229,1717],"canonical_reference":null,"column_id":"notes","content_class":"footnote","geometry_status":"human_verified","hierarchy_level":null,"inline_spans":[],"language":"eng","leaf_id":"single","line_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-native-0024","note_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-note-43","paragraph_role":"continuation","reading_order":24,"source":"human","structure_status":"human_verified","text":"univocal and non-essential to the things that have it, but is not something really existing outside the mind. if Fârâbî","transcription_status":"human_verified","typography_status":"human_verified"},{"bbox":[300,1719,2187,1765],"canonical_reference":null,"column_id":"notes","content_class":"footnote","geometry_status":"human_verified","hierarchy_level":null,"inline_spans":[],"language":"eng","leaf_id":"single","line_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-native-0025","note_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-note-43","paragraph_role":"continuation","reading_order":25,"source":"human","structure_status":"human_verified","text":"and Averroes are right, neither categorial being nor being-as-truth can be by participation as Kindi and Avicenna","transcription_status":"human_verified","typography_status":"human_verified"},{"bbox":[300,1767,2178,1813],"canonical_reference":null,"column_id":"notes","content_class":"footnote","geometry_status":"human_verified","hierarchy_level":null,"inline_spans":[],"language":"eng","leaf_id":"single","line_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-native-0026","note_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-note-43","paragraph_role":"continuation","reading_order":26,"source":"human","structure_status":"human_verified","text":"want; Kindi's and Avicenna's theory is held to depend on a confusion of these two senses of being, which allows","transcription_status":"human_verified","typography_status":"human_verified"},{"bbox":[300,1815,2199,1861],"canonical_reference":null,"column_id":"notes","content_class":"footnote","geometry_status":"human_verified","hierarchy_level":null,"inline_spans":[],"language":"eng","leaf_id":"single","line_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-native-0027","note_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-note-43","paragraph_role":"continuation","reading_order":27,"source":"human","structure_status":"human_verified","text":"them to combine some features of each of them. Thomas basically accepts Averroes' conclusions on the senses of","transcription_status":"human_verified","typography_status":"human_verified"},{"bbox":[300,1863,2256,1909],"canonical_reference":null,"column_id":"notes","content_class":"footnote","geometry_status":"human_verified","hierarchy_level":null,"inline_spans":[],"language":"eng","leaf_id":"single","line_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-native-0028","note_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-note-43","paragraph_role":"continuation","reading_order":28,"source":"human","structure_status":"human_verified","text":"being, but nonetheless wants to hold on to Avicenna's essence-existence distinction; his solution is to call on another","transcription_status":"human_verified","typography_status":"human_verified"},{"bbox":[300,1911,2252,1957],"canonical_reference":null,"column_id":"notes","content_class":"footnote","geometry_status":"human_verified","hierarchy_level":null,"inline_spans":[],"language":"mixed","leaf_id":"single","line_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-native-0029","note_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-note-43","paragraph_role":"continuation","reading_order":29,"source":"human","structure_status":"human_verified","text":"sense of being from Δ7, being-as-actuality, and to concede that being-as-truth is non-real and that categorial being is","transcription_status":"human_verified","typography_status":"human_verified"},{"bbox":[300,1958,2179,2004],"canonical_reference":null,"column_id":"notes","content_class":"footnote","geometry_status":"human_verified","hierarchy_level":null,"inline_spans":[],"language":"eng","leaf_id":"single","line_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-native-0030","note_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-note-43","paragraph_role":"continuation","reading_order":30,"source":"human","structure_status":"human_verified","text":"essential, but to assert that the essence is of itself a potentiality, whose actuality is a real equivocal non-essential","transcription_status":"human_verified","typography_status":"human_verified"},{"bbox":[300,2006,2224,2052],"canonical_reference":null,"column_id":"notes","content_class":"footnote","geometry_status":"human_verified","hierarchy_level":null,"inline_spans":[],"language":"eng","leaf_id":"single","line_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-native-0031","note_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-note-43","paragraph_role":"continuation","reading_order":31,"source":"human","structure_status":"human_verified","text":"existence. (as far as I have been able to find, Avicenna never describes existence as the actuality or activity [fi'l] of","transcription_status":"human_verified","typography_status":"human_verified"},{"bbox":[300,2054,2183,2100],"canonical_reference":null,"column_id":"notes","content_class":"footnote","geometry_status":"human_verified","hierarchy_level":null,"inline_spans":[],"language":"mixed","leaf_id":"single","line_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-native-0032","note_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-note-43","paragraph_role":"continuation","reading_order":32,"source":"human","structure_status":"human_verified","text":"the essence: that seems to be Thomas' innovation). Thomas' interpretation of Δ7 is very dubious: the potentiality","transcription_status":"human_verified","typography_status":"human_verified"},{"bbox":[300,2102,2214,2148],"canonical_reference":null,"column_id":"notes","content_class":"footnote","geometry_status":"human_verified","hierarchy_level":null,"inline_spans":[],"language":"mixed","leaf_id":"single","line_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-native-0033","note_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-note-43","paragraph_role":"continuation","reading_order":33,"source":"human","structure_status":"human_verified","text":"which being-as-actuality completes in Δ7 is something like the stone in which Hermes is potentially present, not a","transcription_status":"human_verified","typography_status":"human_verified"},{"bbox":[300,2150,2206,2196],"canonical_reference":null,"column_id":"notes","content_class":"footnote","geometry_status":"human_verified","hierarchy_level":null,"inline_spans":[],"language":"eng","leaf_id":"single","line_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-native-0034","note_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-note-43","paragraph_role":"continuation","reading_order":34,"source":"human","structure_status":"human_verified","text":"preexistent essence of the Hermes. but what Thomas takes over from Fârâbî and Averroes is also dubious, namely","transcription_status":"human_verified","typography_status":"human_verified"},{"bbox":[300,2198,2250,2244],"canonical_reference":null,"column_id":"notes","content_class":"footnote","geometry_status":"human_verified","hierarchy_level":null,"inline_spans":[],"language":"mixed","leaf_id":"single","line_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-native-0035","note_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-note-43","paragraph_role":"continuation","reading_order":35,"source":"human","structure_status":"human_verified","text":"the identification of existence as analyzed in Posterior Analytics II with being-as-truth as described in Δ7. according","transcription_status":"human_verified","typography_status":"human_verified"},{"bbox":[300,2246,2184,2292],"canonical_reference":null,"column_id":"notes","content_class":"footnote","geometry_status":"human_verified","hierarchy_level":null,"inline_spans":[],"language":"eng","leaf_id":"single","line_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-native-0036","note_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-note-43","paragraph_role":"continuation","reading_order":36,"source":"human","structure_status":"human_verified","text":"to E4, being-as-truth has no external causes, while Posterior Analytics II is emphatic that the cause of the thing's","transcription_status":"human_verified","typography_status":"human_verified"},{"bbox":[300,2294,2143,2340],"canonical_reference":null,"column_id":"notes","content_class":"footnote","geometry_status":"human_verified","hierarchy_level":null,"inline_spans":[],"language":"eng","leaf_id":"single","line_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-native-0037","note_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-note-43","paragraph_role":"continuation","reading_order":37,"source":"human","structure_status":"human_verified","text":"existence is its essence--in fact, existence as described in Posterior Analytics II is per se or categorial being as","transcription_status":"human_verified","typography_status":"human_verified"},{"bbox":[300,2342,2094,2388],"canonical_reference":null,"column_id":"notes","content_class":"footnote","geometry_status":"human_verified","hierarchy_level":null,"inline_spans":[],"language":"mixed","leaf_id":"single","line_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-native-0038","note_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-note-43","paragraph_role":"continuation","reading_order":38,"source":"human","structure_status":"human_verified","text":"described in Δ7. much of what Geach and Owen say about their two senses of being-as-existence, and their","transcription_status":"human_verified","typography_status":"human_verified"},{"bbox":[300,2391,2260,2437],"canonical_reference":null,"column_id":"notes","content_class":"footnote","geometry_status":"human_verified","hierarchy_level":null,"inline_spans":[],"language":"eng","leaf_id":"single","line_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-native-0039","note_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-note-43","paragraph_role":"continuation","reading_order":39,"source":"human","structure_status":"human_verified","text":"downplaying of the Posterior Analytics on existence, seems to be a hangover ultimately from Fârâbî, and to be liable","transcription_status":"human_verified","typography_status":"human_verified"},{"bbox":[300,2439,2160,2485],"canonical_reference":null,"column_id":"notes","content_class":"footnote","geometry_status":"human_verified","hierarchy_level":null,"inline_spans":[],"language":"eng","leaf_id":"single","line_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-native-0040","note_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-note-43","paragraph_role":"continuation","reading_order":40,"source":"human","structure_status":"human_verified","text":"to the same criticisms as his account. {but note that for Fârâbî-Averroes-Thomas, what has being in the weaker","transcription_status":"human_verified","typography_status":"human_verified"},{"bbox":[300,2486,2239,2532],"canonical_reference":null,"column_id":"notes","content_class":"footnote","geometry_status":"human_verified","hierarchy_level":null,"inline_spans":[],"language":"eng","leaf_id":"single","line_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-native-0041","note_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-note-43","paragraph_role":"continuation","reading_order":41,"source":"human","structure_status":"human_verified","text":"sense but not the stronger is e.g. a negation, whereas for Geach and Owen it's e.g. Arrowby who is no more but who","transcription_status":"human_verified","typography_status":"human_verified"},{"bbox":[300,2534,1752,2580],"canonical_reference":null,"column_id":"notes","content_class":"footnote","geometry_status":"human_verified","hierarchy_level":null,"inline_spans":[],"language":"eng","leaf_id":"single","line_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-native-0042","note_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-note-43","paragraph_role":"continuation","reading_order":42,"source":"human","structure_status":"human_verified","text":"still falls under the scope of the existential quantifier; Geach mangles Thomas on this}","transcription_status":"human_verified","typography_status":"human_verified"},{"bbox":[300,2576,2183,2628],"canonical_reference":null,"column_id":"notes","content_class":"footnote","geometry_status":"human_verified","hierarchy_level":null,"inline_spans":[{"bbox":null,"end_char":2,"semantic_role":"none","span_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-native-0043-visual-qa-marker-00","start_char":0,"styles":["superscript"],"target_id":null,"text":"44"}],"language":"mixed","leaf_id":"single","line_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-native-0043","note_id":"menn-metaphysics-pdf337-note-44","paragraph_role":"start","reading_order":43,"source":"human","structure_status":"human_verified","text":"44 some loose ends: note Λ6 on whether motion will be, De Interpretatione c9 on whether a sea-bat